+// MLB Power Pros 2008 (RL8E54): native 8x8 inverse DCTs of the THP movie decoder (Dolphin SDK
+// THPDec: __THPInverseDCTNoYPos 0x80084C7C and __THPInverseDCTY8 0x80085108). The game plays THP
+// video; its MCU-row decoders (__THPDecompressiMCURow512x448 0x80084A30, 0x8008559C, 0x800857EC) call
+// one of these per 8x8 block: six per MCU (4 Y, U, V), four NoYPos and two Y8. Stock-match window
+// profile (local/switch/logs/nxlink-MLBPowerPros2008-20261028-130311.log, windows with the camera
+// on many players): 1.61 + 0.93 ms/frame of the main thread.
+//
+// void IDCT(const s16 coef[64] /* r3 */, u32 xPos /* r4 */): dequantize row by row with the
+// table at *(r13-28672) (64 singles, 8 per coefficient row), a 1-D 8-point transform per row into
+// the 64-float workspace at 0x802B6860 (rows whose coefficients 4-7 / 2-3 / 1 are zero take
+// shortcuts, as many branches of the original), a 1-D transform per column pair out of the
+// workspace (4 iterations of two columns), and u8 stores (psq_st, GQR6 = 0x3D043D04: x * 1/8,
+// truncated, clamped to 0..255; NaN -> 0) into the plane at *(r13-28608): rows of 8 bytes, the
+// 8 rows of the block as two 4-row halves at r6 and r7. Per-plane stride *(r13-28640) is 512 (Y)
+// or 256 (U, V) in the 512x448 decoder. NoYPos: out + (xPos << 2); Y8 adds 8 rows of the stride
+// (stride << 3). Constants (singles at r2-30792: f29 f28 f27 f26 f25) are the IDCT's rotation
+// factors and the rounding/level bias f25 added to the DC terms.
+//
+// The translation computes every pair with the ps helpers (a NaN resolver per op), checks and
+// resolves each memory range, byte-swaps each access, and keeps CR0 and the 24 temporaries
+// through its register file. Here pass 1 (the eight row transforms, with the branches, CR0 and
+// registers of the original: a transliteration) is the same operations in the same order as single
+// NEON instructions on float32x2_t (lane 1 = ps0, lane 0 = ps1 as ppc_isa_float.h), and pass 2
+// does the translation's four column-pair iterations at once on float32x4_t (the ops are
+// lane-wise: a column's result does not depend on its neighbours) with the 8 output rows stored as
+// 8-byte vectors. Guest memory goes through the flat view with one rev per access, the constants
+// are hoisted, and the exit state the translation leaves is reproduced: r0, r3-r8, r10, CR0, CTR,
+// f0-f13 (r1 and f25-f31 return unchanged; the translation never writes the callee-saved slots,
+// only the back chain at r1-128). Instruction count per call (qemu, a typical sparse block): 4240
+// translated -> 1220 here, dense block 5600 -> 1660.
+//
+// Why plain NEON gives the translation's bits: every pair op is IEEE single arithmetic per lane
+// (vadd/vsub/vmul, vfma for ps_madd/msub/nmsub as PpcFmaddPairInline/PpcFmsubPairInline); the
+// translation's NaN resolver acts only on NaN lanes. A NaN or infinity cannot arise from finite
+// bounded inputs (|s16| <= 2^15, |table| < 2^23, |constant| < 2^8: no intermediate exceeds 2^105),
+// so the fast path requires exactly that of the 64 table entries and the 5 constants (a
+// constant must also not be subnormal: PsFromScalar's double -> single narrowing flushes it under
+// FZ, a compiler-dependent detail) and runs the translation otherwise. Subnormal products are
+// left to the hardware as in the translation (same FPCR.FZ). The workspace holds singles through
+// psq_st type 0 (subnormal -> signed zero), the output goes through the U8 scale-61 quantizer.
+//
+// Fast path conditions, checked at entry (else the translation runs the whole call; the back
+// chain store it starts with has been done and is idempotent): flat view, GQR0 = 0, no wrap of
+// any source range (constants, parameter block, coefficients, table), none of them overlaps the
+// workspace, both output ranges (rows of the two halves, 38 bytes) are inside no wrap, outside
+// the MMIO window (0xCC000000-0xCDFFFFFF), disjoint from each other and from the workspace (so the
+// order of the 64 output stores, which differs from the translation's, is immaterial). Table: only its
+// 256 bytes are read, all of them (the translation reads fewer when rows are zero; a table in
+// readable memory is a given for the game).
+//
+// This file builds like the translated code (-O2 -fno-fast-math -ffp-contract=off, outside the
+// unity build: runtime/CMakeLists.txt, as mtx_natives.cpp).
+#if defined(__SWITCH__)
+#include <arm_neon.h>
+#include <cstdint>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
